1. include/factor_builders/sonar_range_residual.hpp, src/factor_builders/sonar_range_residual.cpp
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ported from:
  SVIn (AutonomousFieldRoboticsLab/SVIn), repository license: GPLv3.
  okvis_ros/okvis/okvis_ceres/include/okvis/ceres/SonarError.hpp
  okvis_ros/okvis/okvis_ceres/src/SonarError.cpp

Upstream file-level copyright (retained verbatim in the ported files):
  Copyright (c) 2015, Autonomous Systems Lab / ETH Zurich (OKVIS base,
  BSD-3-Clause file header) — SonarError itself authored by Sharmin Rahman
  for SVIn (combined work distributed under SVIn's repository-level GPLv3).

What was ported: the 1-D sonar range residual formulation — given a pose
T_WS and a subset of nearby landmarks, residual = sqrt(information) *
(measured_range - ||T_WS.translation() - mean(landmarkSubset)||) — and its
analytic Jacobian with respect to the pose translation. This is the "sonar
constrains distance to a landmark cluster, never fabricates elevation"
pattern referenced in acoustic-optic-slam-platform-architecture-2026-08-17.md
sections 6/21.

What was NOT ported: SVIn's Ceres SizedCostFunction wiring, its VIO/OKVIS
internal state representation, or any other SVIn source file. The residual
math was re-expressed against this repository's own backend-agnostic
ResidualBlock interface (see include/measurement_api), not against Ceres.

