2. include/frontends/{cfar_detector,dbscan,sonar_cfar_frontend}.hpp,
   src/frontends/{cfar_detector,dbscan,sonar_cfar_frontend}.cpp
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ported from:
  sonar_camera_reconstruction (ivanacollg/sonar_camera_reconstruction),
  repository license: MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Ivana Collado.
  sonar_camera_reconstruction_pkg/scripts/CFAR.py
  sonar_camera_reconstruction_pkg/scripts/imaging_sonar.py

What was ported: the CFAR detector (CA/SOCA/GOCA/OS threshold-factor
derivations and cell-averaging test), the polar-to-Cartesian remap table
construction (generate_map_xy), first-contact line-scan extraction
(extract_line_scan), and DBSCAN-based scanline clustering
(cluster_scanline).

What was deliberately NOT ported: merge.py's rotate_cloud/merge_data
world-frame baking, which discards pitch (uses roll+yaw only) and bakes
points directly into the `map` frame. This repository's frontend instead
stops at sonar-local-frame range-bearing evidence
(MeasurementEvidence<SonarRangeBearing>) per the platform architecture's
contract that frontends own measurement evidence, not global pose/map
state (acoustic-optic-slam-platform-architecture-2026-08-17.md section 21,
item 1; and section 22.1's audit finding on the pitch-discard issue).

